        "original_id": "5e5bb4b9-2297-5ee6-b59b-18932d11e3d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Higgins Creek, Kioloa State Forest, Batemans Bay, southern New South Wales, South Coast, Deua National Park, Moruya, Narooma, Congo, Eurobodalla Shire, Australia\n- Species: Cortinarius kioloensis\n\nFacts:\n- The type specimen of Cortinarius kioloensis was collected along Higgins Creek in Kioloa State Forest near Batemans Bay in southern New South Wales on 22 June 1980.\n- Batemans Bay is a town in the South Coast region of New South Wales, Australia.\n- The nearest coastal towns to Deua National Park are Batemans Bay, Moruya, and Narooma.\n- Congo is a village in Eurobodalla Shire on the South Coast of New South Wales.",
